inline.body:
`shape` is an object literal, so `key in shape` is `true` for every `Object.prototype` member regardless of what `properties` declared. `required: ["toString"]`, `["constructor"]`, `["valueOf"]` and friends are therefore silently skipped and never enforced — I confirmed `{ type: "object", required: ["constructor"], additionalProperties: { type: "string" } }` accepts `{}`.

No prototype-pollution risk (the assignment is skipped rather than performed), but the constraint is dropped.

```suggestion
      // `required` may name keys `properties` never declares. Their values fall to
      // `additionalProperties`, but they still have to be present.
      for (const key of requiredSet) {
        if (!Object.hasOwn(shape, key)) shape[key] = additionalSchema ?? z.any();
```

